WEBVTT

00:00:05.281 --> 00:00:08.821
So far, we have explored what conversational AI

00:00:08.821 --> 00:00:12.000
is and how it works behind the scenes.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
The next step is understanding how these capabilities are applied in real

00:00:18.025 --> 00:00:19.160
organizations.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.000
In practice, not all conversational AI systems are

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.200
built the same.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.782
They differ in how much they can understand, how flexible they are,

00:00:29.782 --> 00:00:32.720
and how much responsibility they can take on.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:38.635
These differences matter because choosing the right type of system has a direct

00:00:38.635 --> 00:00:41.760
impact on cost, risk, and business outcomes.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.942
To make sense of this, conversational AI can be grouped into 3

00:00:47.942 --> 00:00:54.880
broad categories, traditional chat bots, AI chat bots and agentic AI chat bots.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.360
Traditional chat bots are the simplest form of conversational systems.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.640
They rely on predefined rules and keyword based logic.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.200
Conversations follow scripted paths, often built using decision trees.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:15.037
A user asks a question and the chat bot matches it to a known pattern before

00:01:15.037 --> 00:01:17.000
delivering a fixed response.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:22.073
Because of this design, traditional chat bots are usually limited

00:01:22.073 --> 00:01:23.920
to single turn interactions.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:30.484
They work best for predictable and repetitive tasks such as FAQs or basic

00:01:30.484 --> 00:01:32.200
information requests.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.620
However, they struggle when users phrase questions

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.840
differently or need to provide additional context.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.585
AI chat bots use language models to understand nuance, synonyms,

00:01:44.585 --> 00:01:46.120
and varied phrasing.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:51.683
Instead of relying on rigid scripts, they generate responses dynamically based

00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:53.200
on intent and context.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:59.659
Conversations can span multiple turns, allowing users to ask follow up questions

00:01:59.659 --> 00:02:01.480
or refine their requests.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:04.964
Naturally, AI chat bots are well suited for handling

00:02:04.964 --> 00:02:09.040
A broader range of simple to moderately complex interactions.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.459
Over time, they also improve by learning from

00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:15.120
conversation patterns and user feedback.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:20.977
Agentic AI chat bots are advanced systems that go beyond understanding and

00:02:20.977 --> 00:02:21.760
responding.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:27.911
They are designed to take action Agentic AI chat bots can use additional inputs

00:02:27.911 --> 00:02:33.080
such as conversation history, user context, or uploaded information.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:36.660
They can trigger workflows, make decisions,

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.480
and complete tasks from start to finish.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.800
Instead of stopping at an answer, these systems focus on outcomes.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.468
They adapt their behavior based on results and learn from the actions they

00:02:50.468 --> 00:02:53.533
take, allowing them to operate with a higher

00:02:53.533 --> 00:02:54.760
level of autonomy.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:01.171
Understanding the different types of conversational AI is only part of the

00:03:01.171 --> 00:03:03.720
picture in real organizations.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.880
The next challenge is deciding how to implement these systems effectively.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:15.446
Some organizations choose to build conversational AI systems entirely on

00:03:15.446 --> 00:03:16.280
their own.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:20.640
This approach offers maximum control and customization,

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.854
but it also requires strong engineering capability, ongoing maintenance,

00:03:25.854 --> 00:03:27.640
and long term investment.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:34.161
It is best suited for organizations with a proven track record of building complex

00:03:34.161 --> 00:03:35.480
internal platforms.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:41.933
Another approach is to build solutions using frameworks provided by large cloud

00:03:41.933 --> 00:03:42.640
platforms.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:47.687
This reduces development effort and integrates more easily with existing

00:03:47.687 --> 00:03:48.960
enterprise systems.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.953
However, it also creates dependency on a specific

00:03:51.953 --> 00:03:55.860
technology stack and still requires specialized skills to customize and

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.000
support the solution.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:01.402
Alternatively, many organizations choose to work with

00:04:01.402 --> 00:04:03.560
conversational AI specialists.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:09.680
This approach accelerates deployment and reduces the need for in house expertise.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.617
In some cases, industry specific models can further

00:04:14.617 --> 00:04:16.240
reduce time and cost.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:20.120
The trade off is reduced control over the solution.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:24.920
There is no single right approach to conversational AI.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:31.520
The most successful implementations align with how an organization already works.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:37.072
Companies that thrive on internal development may succeed by building in

00:04:37.072 --> 00:04:37.480
house.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.360
Others perform better by partnering with specialists.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:46.524
For corporate teams, the real value lies in understanding the

00:04:46.524 --> 00:04:51.899
options, recognizing tradeoffs, and choosing an approach that fits their

00:04:51.899 --> 00:04:55.360
organizations capabilities and business goals.